From 742eff89d592e3f91ea5652f13cb6461a400ca8b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: kalyan alle <kalyan.alle@intel.com>
Date: Wed, 13 May 2026 08:50:51 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] vfio/i915: Add default handler for .match_token_uuid

Commit 86624ba3b522 ("vfio/pci: Do vf_token checks for
VFIO_DEVICE_BIND_IOMMUFD") split VF-token validation out of
vfio_pci_core_match() into a new .match_token_uuid device op, which
vfio_pci_core_match() now calls unconditionally. All in-tree vfio-pci
variants were updated; the out-of-tree i915-vfio-pci variant was missed.

Opening an i915 SR-IOV VF from QEMU therefore hits a NULL function
pointer in vfio_pci_core_match() and Oopses the host, freezing the guest:

  BUG: kernel NULL pointer dereference, address: 0000000000000000
  RIP: 0010:0x0
   vfio_pci_core_match+0x133/0x1a0 [vfio_pci_core]
   vfio_group_fops_unl_ioctl+0x15c/0x7d0 [vfio]

Wire up the standard helper vfio_pci_core_match_token_uuid in
i915_vfio_pci_ops, matching every other in-tree vfio-pci driver.

Fixes: 86624ba3b522 ("vfio/pci: Do vf_token checks for VFIO_DEVICE_BIND_IOMMUFD")
Signed-off-by: kalyan alle <kalyan.alle@intel.com>
---
 drivers/vfio/pci/i915/main.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/drivers/vfio/pci/i915/main.c b/drivers/vfio/pci/i915/main.c
index b56f9b1f47b1..e5914a5bd9ba 100644
--- a/drivers/vfio/pci/i915/main.c
+++ b/drivers/vfio/pci/i915/main.c
@@ -346,6 +346,7 @@ static const struct vfio_device_ops i915_vfio_pci_ops = {
 	.mmap		= vfio_pci_core_mmap,
 	.request	= vfio_pci_core_request,
 	.match		= vfio_pci_core_match,
+	.match_token_uuid = vfio_pci_core_match_token_uuid,
 	.bind_iommufd	= vfio_iommufd_physical_bind,
 	.unbind_iommufd = vfio_iommufd_physical_unbind,
 	.attach_ioas	= vfio_iommufd_physical_attach_ioas,
-- 
2.34.1

